hadiths[51]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1348","‘Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) says that some people from Banu Tamim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: “O people of Banu Tamim! Rejoice.” They said, “You have given us glad tidings, now (give us some wealth as well).” Upon this, the color of the blessed face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed. Then some people from Yemen came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: “O people of Yemen! Accept the glad tidings, for Banu Tamim did not accept it.” They said, “We have accepted.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to speak about the beginning of creation and the Throne. Meanwhile, a man came and said (to me), “O Imran! Your she-camel has gotten loose (go and catch it).” I got up and left, but in my heart remained the regret that I wish I had not gotten up."
"1349","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates in one narration that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah was, and there was nothing besides Him, and His Throne was upon the water, and He wrote everything in the Preserved Tablet, and He created the heavens and the earth...."" Then a man called out, ""O Ibn Husain! Your she-camel has gotten loose,"" so I went away, but the she-camel had gone beyond the mirage (that sand which shines like water in the sunlight). By Allah, I wished that I had left the she-camel and not gotten up from there."
"1350","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: 'The son of Adam abuses Me, and it is not befitting for him to abuse Me, and he denies Me, and it is not befitting for him. His abusing Me is his saying that I have a child, and his denying Me is his saying that I will not resurrect him as I created him the first time.'"""
"1351","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Allah created the creation, He wrote in His Book, which is with Him above the Throne: 'My mercy prevails over My wrath.'"""
"1352","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Time has come back to its original state as it was on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth. The year is twelve months, of which four are sacred; three are consecutive: Dhu al-Qa'dah, Dhu al-Hijjah, Muharram, and (the fourth) Rajab of Mudar (the tribe of Mudar used to venerate it greatly), which is between Jumada al-Thani and Sha'ban."""
"1353","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Dharr while the sun was setting: ""Do you know where this (sun) goes?"" I said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He (peace be upon him) said: ""It goes and prostrates under the Throne, then seeks permission (from Allah) to rise (from the east), so it is granted permission. And soon a time will come when it will prostrate, but its prostration will not be accepted, and it will seek permission but will not be granted permission. Rather, it will be told: 'Return from where you came.' So it will rise from the west. This is the meaning of Allah Almighty's statement: 'And the sun runs on its fixed course, that is the decree of the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing.' (Surah Ya-Sin: 38)."""
"1354","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: On the Day of Resurrection, the sun and the moon will be folded up (they will lose their light)."
"1355","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a patch of cloud in the sky, he would sometimes move forward, sometimes step back, sometimes go inside, sometimes come outside, and the color of his blessed face would change. Then, when it started to rain, that state of his (peace be upon him) would go away. Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) asked the reason for this, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How do I know? Perhaps this is not the cloud about which, when the people of 'Ad saw it approaching their valleys, they said, 'This is a cloud bringing us rain...' (Surah Al-Ahqaf: 24)"""
"1356","Sayyiduna Ya'la (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting this verse on the pulpit: ""And they will call out, 'O Malik...'"" (Surah Az-Zukhruf: 77) (Malik is the name of the keeper of Hell)."
"1357","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: The night I was taken on the Mi'raj, I saw Musa (peace be upon him), who was a wheat-colored, tall man with curly hair, resembling the people of the tribe of Shanu’ah. And I also saw Isa (peace be upon him), who was of medium height, medium build, reddish-white, with straight hair. And I saw the angel who is the keeper of Hell. And I saw the Dajjal among the signs of Allah that Allah showed me (on that day). And (in Surah As-Sajdah: 23) where it is said, ""You should not have any doubt about this meeting,"" (it refers to the meeting with Musa (peace be upon him) on the night of Mi'raj)."
"1358","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us, and he is the truthful and the believed: “The creation of each one of you is completed in his mother’s womb. For forty days he remains as a drop of fluid, then for the same period as a clot of blood, then for the same number of days as a lump of flesh. Then Allah sends an angel, and he is commanded regarding four matters: (1) it is said to him to write his deeds, (2) his provision, (3) his lifespan, (4) and (to write) whether he is wretched or blessed (i.e., fortunate or unfortunate). Then the soul is breathed into him. So, indeed, one of you may perform deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only a cubit between him and Paradise, then the decree (written destiny) overtakes him and he begins to do the deeds of the people of Hellfire and thus enters it. And a person may perform deeds of the people of Hellfire until there is only a cubit between him and Hell, then the decree (destiny) overtakes him and he begins to do the deeds of the people of Paradise and thus enters it.”"
"1359","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibreel (peace be upon him) and says: 'Allah loves so-and-so, so you should also love him.' So Jibreel (peace be upon him) begins to love him. Then Jibreel (peace be upon him) announces among the inhabitants of the heavens that Allah loves so-and-so, so you should also love him. Thus, all the inhabitants of the heavens begin to love him, and then acceptance for him is placed among the people of the earth."""
"1360","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The angels descend in the clouds and mention the commands of Allah that have been decreed in the heavens on that day. Then the devils secretly listen to it and come to the soothsayers and convey it to them, and they add some lies from themselves to it."""
"1361","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When it is Friday, angels stand at every door of the mosque and record the names of those who come, in order of their arrival. The one who comes first, then the one who comes after him, and so on. When the Imam sits (on the pulpit), they close their registers and come to listen to the sermon."""
"1362","Narrated Al-Bara' (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Satirize the polytheists, and Gabriel (peace be upon him) is with you."""
"1363","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said to her: ""O Aisha! This is Jibreel (Gabriel, peace be upon him) who conveys greetings to you."" She replied, ""And peace be upon him, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. You (peace be upon you) see what I do not see."" By ""tarā"" (you see), the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was meant."
"1364","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibreel (peace be upon him): ""Why do you not come to us more often than you do?"" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: Then this verse was revealed: ""And we (angels) do not descend except by the command of your Lord. To Him belongs whatever is before us and whatever is behind us."" (Surah Maryam: 64)"
"1365","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Gabriel (peace be upon him) taught me the Qur'an in one mode of recitation, then I kept asking him for more until it reached seven modes of recitation."""
"1366","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), “Has there been any day harder upon you than the day of Uhud?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: “The troubles I have faced from your people (the Quraysh), only I know them, and the hardest day I faced was the day of Aqabah (which is towards Ta’if), when I presented myself to Ibn Abd Yalail bin Abd Kulal (who was the chief of Ta’if), and he did not fulfill my wish. So I left in great distress, and I did not come to my senses until I reached Qarn al-Tha’alib (a place). I raised my head and saw that a piece of cloud was shading me. Then I looked and saw that in it was Jibreel (peace be upon him). He called out to me that Allah has heard the words of your people to you and the response they gave you, and Allah has sent the Angel of the Mountains to you, so you may command him regarding the disbelievers as you wish.” Then the Angel of the Mountains called out to me, greeted me with peace, and then said, “O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! Whatever you wish is present. If you wish, I will cause the two mountains of Akhshabayn to fall upon them?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: “No! I do not wish that. Rather, I hope that Allah will bring forth from their descendants people who will worship Allah alone and not associate anything with Him.”"
"1367","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them)` explains the meaning of this verse: ""Then he drew near, and came closer, till he was at a distance of two bow-lengths or even nearer. So He revealed to His servant what He revealed."" That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Jibreel (Gabriel) (peace be upon him) in his original form; he had six hundred wings. (Surah An-Najm: 9-10)"
"1368","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that (regarding Surah An-Najm, verse: 18) ""Indeed, he saw of the greatest signs of his Lord."" (The meaning is that) the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a green carpet which covered the edges of the sky. (Upon it was Jibreel (peace be upon him) sitting, or it was on his wings.)"
"1369","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: Whoever thinks that Muhammad (peace be upon him) saw his Lord has thought wrongly; rather, the Prophet (peace be upon him) saw Jibreel (Gabriel) (peace be upon him) in his (original) form and creation, who had filled the horizons of the sky."
"1370","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a husband calls his wife to bed and she refuses, and he goes to sleep angry with her, the angels curse her until morning."""
"1371","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you dies, his place is shown to him morning and evening; if he is among the people of Paradise, then his place in Paradise is shown to him, and if he is among the people of Hell, then his place in Hell is shown to him."""
"1372","Narrated by Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""I saw in Paradise, and most of its people were (those who were poor, needy, and) destitute in the world, and I saw in Hell, and among the people of Hell I saw a majority of women."""
"1373","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): One day we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said: ""While I was sleeping, I saw myself in Paradise, and there was a woman performing ablution in the corner of a palace. I asked, 'Whose palace is this?' The people said, 'It belongs to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him).' So I remembered his sense of honor and turned away."" Upon hearing this, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) began to weep and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Would I feel any sense of honor (ghirah) towards you?"""
"1374","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The very first group to enter Paradise will have faces as bright as the full moon. They will neither spit, nor blow their noses, nor defecate therein. Their utensils will be of gold, and their combs will be of gold and silver, and in their braziers aloes-wood will burn, and their sweat will be like musk (i.e., as fragrant as musk). Each of them will have two beautiful and delicate wives, the marrow of whose shins will be visible from beneath the flesh. There will be no differences or enmity among the people of Paradise; their hearts will be as one, and they will glorify Allah morning and evening."""
"1375","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The very first group to enter Paradise will have faces shining like the full moon, and those who enter after them will shine like the brightest star. The hearts of all of them will be like the heart of a single person (due to mutual love); there will be no differences or enmity among them. Each of them will have two beautiful and delicate wives, whose shinbones will be visible from within the flesh. They will glorify Allah morning and evening; they will never fall ill, nor will they blow their noses, nor spit... and the rest of the hadith has been narrated which has already passed (see the previous hadith)."""
"1376","Sahih Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: “Indeed, seventy thousand people from my Ummah, or (he said) seven hundred thousand people, will enter Paradise together (not one after another), whose faces will shine like the moon on the fourteenth night.”"
"1377","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): A cloak made of sundus (silk cloth) was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he used to forbid the use of silk cloth. The people began to admire it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the handkerchiefs of Sa'd bin Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) in Paradise are better than this."""
"1378","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""In Paradise, there is a tree such that if a rider were to travel in its shade for a hundred years, he would still not be able to cross it (this tree is Tuba)."""
"1379","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider could travel for a hundred years and not reach the end of it. And if you wish, recite this verse: 'And extended shade.' (Surah Al-Waqi'ah: 30)"""
"1380","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He (peace be upon him) said, ""The people of Paradise will look at those above them as you see a shining star on the horizon of the east or the west, because some (people of Paradise) will be superior to others."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! These are the stations of the Prophets; how can anyone else reach them?"" He (peace be upon him) said, ""(Why) not! By Him in Whose hand is my soul, there will be people who believed in Allah and affirmed the truth of the Messengers (who will also reach there)."""
"1381","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), the truthful, narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: “Fever is from the boiling of Hell, so cool it with water.”"
"1382","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The heat of your fire is one part out of seventy parts of the heat of the Fire of Hell."" It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The fire of this world would have been sufficient for burning."" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has been increased by sixty-nine parts, each part as hot as it."""
"1383","Sayyiduna Usamah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""On the Day of Resurrection, a man will be brought and he will be thrown into the Fire. Then his intestines will come out in the Fire and he will revolve around them as a donkey revolves around a millstone. Then the people of Hell will gather around him and say, 'O so-and-so! What is the matter with you? Did you not used to enjoin us to do good and forbid us from evil?' He will say, 'Yes, I used to enjoin you to do good but I did not do it myself, and I used to forbid you from evil but I used to do it myself.'"""
"1384","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that (on one occasion) magic was done on the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) (the effect of which was) that he (peace be upon him) would think he had done something, although he had not done it. Eventually, one day he (peace be upon him) made supplication and prayed a lot. After that, he (peace be upon him) said (to me): “Do you know that Allah has informed me of the matter in which is my cure? Two men came to me, one sat by my head and the other by my feet. Then one of them asked the other, ‘What is the illness of this man?’ The other replied, ‘Magic has been done on him.’ He asked, ‘Who has done magic on him?’ The other said, ‘Labeed bin A’sam (the Jew).’ He asked, ‘In what (thing)?’ The other said, ‘In a comb, hair, and the outer skin of a male date palm’s cluster.’ He asked, ‘Where is it?’ The other said, ‘In the well named Dharwan.’” So the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) went there. When he returned from there, he (peace be upon him) said to Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): “The trees near that (well) are as if they are the heads of devils.” (Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, says) I asked, “Did you have it taken out?” He (peace be upon him) replied, “No. Allah has cured me, and (in having it taken out) I feared that it would cause mischief among the people (and the talk of magic would spread more).” After that, the well was closed."
"1385","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Satan comes to one of you and says (i.e., puts a whisper), 'Who created this?' and 'Who created that?' until he says, 'Tell me, who created your Lord?' So when it comes to this point, that person should recite 'A'udhu billah' (I seek refuge with Allah) and abandon such satanic thoughts."""
"1386","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointing towards the east and saying, ""Trials and tribulations will emerge from this direction, trials and tribulations will emerge from this direction, from where the horn of Satan appears."""
"1387","Narrated by Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""When the darkness of night falls, keep your children inside the house, for at that time the devils spread out. When an hour of the night prayer (Isha) has passed, then let the children go (to walk around). And close your door by saying 'Bismillah' (in the name of Allah), and extinguish your lamp by saying 'Bismillah' (i.e., extinguish every kind of fire), and cover your water vessel (pitcher, cooler, underground tank, etc.) by saying 'Bismillah'. If you do not find anything to cover it with, then place a stick or something similar over it."""
"1388","Sayyiduna Sulaiman bin Surad (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was sitting with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and two men were abusing each other. One of them's face turned red with anger and his veins swelled. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""I know a supplication, if this person recites it, his anger will go away. If he says: 'A'udhu billahi minash-shaytanir-rajim' (I seek refuge with Allah from the accursed devil), his anger will depart."" So the people said to that person that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) has said this, so seek refuge with Allah from the devil! He said: ""Am I mad (that I should seek refuge from the devil)?"" (Perhaps this person was an ignorant villager or a hypocrite, so he did not accept this advice.)"
"1389","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Yawning is from the devil, so when one of you feels like yawning, he should try to restrain it as much as possible, because when one of you says 'Ha' while yawning, the devil laughs."""
"1390","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A good dream is from Allah and a bad dream is from Satan. So when any of you sees a bad dream (a dream that frightens him), he should spit on his left side (three times) and seek refuge in Allah from its evil, then that (dream) will not harm him."""
"1391","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When any one of you wakes up from sleep and performs ablution, he should blow his nose three times, for the devil spends the night at the upper part of his nose."""
"1392","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying from the pulpit in a sermon: ""Kill snakes wherever you find them, and do not leave alive the two (white) striped ones and the one with a cut tail, for they cause blindness and cause pregnant women to miscarry."" Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was chasing a snake to kill it when Abu Lubabah (may Allah be pleased with him) called out to me (and said): Do not kill it. So I said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has ordered us to kill snakes. He said: Indeed, but after that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing house snakes. (Az-Zuhri said:) Such snakes are called 'al-'awamir' (because they stay in the house for a long time, they are called 'awamir', meaning long-lived ones)."
"1393","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Some people among the Children of Israel disappeared; no one knew what they had done. Their forms were transformed. I think that those people became mice, because if camel's milk is placed before a mouse, it does not drink it (in the religion of the Children of Israel, the camel was forbidden), but if goat's milk is placed, it drinks it."" So I (Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith to Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said, ""Did you hear this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"" I said, ""Yes."" (Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him) kept asking me the same thing repeatedly, so I said, ""(If I had not heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him,) then do I read the Torah?"""
"1394","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The peak of disbelief is towards the east, and pride and arrogance are among the horsemen, camel riders, and landowners, while tranquility and contentment are among the shepherds of goats."""
"1395","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amr Abu Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed with his hand towards Yemen and then said: “(True) faith is in Yemen. Harshness and hard-heartedness (cruelty) are among those people who drive the camels by holding their tails.” (Then he pointed towards the east and said:) “From where the horns of Satan will emerge, that is, among the tribes of Rabi’ah and Mudar (there will be harshness and cruelty).”"
"1396","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear the rooster crowing (giving the call), then ask Allah for His bounty and grace, because (at that time) the rooster sees an angel. And when you hear the braying of a donkey, then seek refuge with Allah from Satan, because (at that time) it sees Satan."""
"1397","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a fly falls into the drink of any one of you, he should dip it in, then take it out, for on one of its wings is disease and on the other is cure."""
"1398","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Allah forgave a sinful woman only because she saw a dog panting at the mouth of a well, about to die of thirst. So she took off her shoe, tied it with her scarf, drew water from the well for the dog, and gave it to drink. Allah, in return for this good deed, saved her from Hell."""
